{"step_index":154,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T14:13:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-01T19:43:57+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-01T19:43:57+05:30\nShowing lines 15-45 of 56\n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 📂 Repository Context & Reference Files\n18: - [docs/setup-guide.md](docs/setup-guide.md): Step-by-step instructions for getting Telegram API credentials, Bot Token, Private Log Channel, and MongoDB Atlas URI.\n19: - [docs/architecture-plan.md](docs/architecture-plan.md): Full technical architecture, component flowcharts, and module breakdown.\n20: - `conversations/`: Full directory copy containing transcripts, raw step logs, and previous design artifacts.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 📋 Confirmed Design Decisions (From `/grill-me` Interview)\n25: - **Primary Source:** Public Telegram channel scraping (bootstraps with a channel list on startup + `/index @channel` command).\n26: - **Secondary Source:** Torrent fallback for unindexed movies with high-seed torrent lookups.\n27: - **File Sizing:** Shows all resolutions (up to 4K). Files exceeding 1.99 GB are automatically split into parts using `ffmpeg` stream copying (no re-encoding) to comply with Telegram's free 2 GB upload limit.\n28: - **User Interface:** Interactive inline button search results. Selecting an item delivers the Telegram video file with the direct streaming link in the caption.\n29: - **Security:** Private whitelist only (`ALLOWED_USERS` in `.env`).\n30: - **Initial Target:** Tested locally on PC first, designed cleanly for future 24/7 cloud deployment (e.g. Oracle Cloud Always-Free or Linux VPS).\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 🚀 Exact Prompt to Continue Development\n35: \n36: When you open this project in **Antigravity** (or another AI coding agent) on your PC, paste this exact prompt:\n37: \n38: ```text\n39: I am continuing development on stream-vault (d:\\Direct_Link). \n40: Please read CONTINUE.md, docs/setup-guide.md, and docs/architecture-plan.md to understand the architecture and confirmed requirements. \n41: Let's proceed with Step 1 of the implementation plan:\n42: 1. Create the PowerShell dependency checker (scripts/check_dependencies.ps1) for Python, ffmpeg, and aria2c.\n43: 2. Create requirements.txt and .env.example.\n44: 3. Build config.py and the asynchronous MongoDB database client in bot/utils/database.py.\n45: ```"}
