{"step_index":172,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T14:16:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-01T19:46:56+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-01T19:46:57+05:30\nThe tool's output was truncated due to being too long. You can find the full output in a file at file:///C:/Users/int-vasanth/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a01f3378-859c-4460-83c1-fd265a9ee6b1/.system_generated/steps/172/output.txt.\n\nHere is a preview with the middle of the output truncated:\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n.env.example:MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript/00000000.jsonl:{\"step_index\":25,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-01T13:34:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":2543,\"cache_read_tokens\":27184,\"output_tokens\":804,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"ArtifactMetadata\":\"{\\\"RequestFeedback\\\":false,\\\"Summary\\\":\\\"Step-by-step walkthrough to get Telegram Bot Token, Telegram API ID & Hash, Private Storage Channel, and Free MongoDB Atlas URI for the Hybrid Movie Bot.\\\",\\\"UserFacing\\\":true}\",\"Content\":\"\\\"# Telegram & MongoDB Credentials Setup Walkthrough\\\\n\\\\nThis guide details how to obtain the necessary credentials to build and run your **Hybrid Telegram Movie Bot**.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Telegram Bot Token (@BotFather)\\\\n1. Open Telegram and search for **`@BotFather`**.\\\\n2. Send `/newbot`.\\\\n3. Provide a display name (e.g., `My Movie Streamer`) and a bot username ending in `bot` (e.g., `my_movie_streamer_bot`).\\\\n4. Copy the HTTP API token provided (e.g., `1234567890:ABCdefGhIJKlmNoPQRsTUVwxyZ`).\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Telegram API ID & API Hash (my.telegram.org)\\\\n1. Navigate to [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org) in a web browser.\\\\n2. Sign in with your Telegram phone number and verify via the in-app code.\\\\n3. Click on **API development tools**.\\\\n4. Fill in an app title and short name (e.g., `MovieScraper`).\\\\n5. Copy the generated **`App api_id`** and **`App api_hash`**.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Private Storage / Log Channel\\\\n1. In Telegram, create a **New Private Channel** (e.g., `Movie Storage Vault`).\\\\n2. Add your newly created bot as an **Administrator** with full permissions.\\\\n3. Obtain the Channel ID (starts with `-100`, e.g., `-1001987654321`) by forwarding a channel post to `@userinfobot`.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Free MongoDB Atlas Cluster\\\\n1. Sign up at [mongodb.com/cloud/atlas](https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register).\\\\n2. Create a free deployment (**M0 Free Shared** tier).\\\\n3. Under Database Access, create a username and strong password.\\\\n4. Under Network Access, add `0.0.0.0/0` (Allow access from anywhere).\\\\n5. In Cluster view, click **Connect** → **Drivers** (Python) and copy the connection URI string.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Configuration Reference (`.env`)\\\\n```env\\\\nAPI_ID=your_api_id\\\\nAPI_HASH=your_api_hash\\\\nBOT_TOKEN=your_bot_token\\\\nLOG_CHANNEL_ID=-100xxxxxxxxxx\\\\nMONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\\\\n```\\\\n\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"Path\":\"\\\"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\int-vasanth\\\\\\\\.gemini\\\\\\\\antigravity\\\\\\\\brain\\\\\\\\a01f3378-859c-4460-83c1-fd265a9ee6b1\\\\\\\\credentials-setup-guide.md\\\"\"}}]}\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript/00000001.jsonl:{\"step_index\":101,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-01T14:09:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":2424,\"cache_read_tokens\":59451,\"output_tokens\":437,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"Content\":\"\\\"# Telegram API Credentials (from https://my.telegram.org)\\\\nAPI_ID=12345678\\\\nAPI_HASH=your_api_hash_here\\\\n\\\\n# Telegram Bot Token (from @BotFather)\\\\nBOT_TOKEN=1234567890:ABCdefGhIJKlmNoPQRsTUVwxyZ\\\\n\\\\n# Private Channel ID for permanent media storage (e.g. -1001234567890)\\\\nLOG_CHANNEL_ID=-1001234567890\\\\n\\\\n# MongoDB Atlas Connection URI\\\\nMONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\\\\nDATABASE_NAME=stream_vault\\\\n\\\\n# Whitelist Security: Comma-separated list of Telegram User IDs allowed to use the bot\\\\nALLOWED_USERS=123456789,987654321\\\\n\\\\n# Web Server Configuration for Direct Download / Streaming Links (DDL)\\\\n# For Hugging Face Spaces, PORT is 7860\\\\nPORT=7860\\\\nHOST=0.0.0.0\\\\n# Public base URL used to construct the streaming link in captions\\\\n# For Hugging Face Spaces: https://<username>-<spacename>.hf.space\\\\n# For local testing: http://localhost:7860\\\\nSTREAM_URL=http://localhost:7860\\\\n\\\\n# Optional: Comma-separated channel usernames to auto-index on startup\\\\n# e.g., @public_movie_channel_1, @public_movie_channel_2\\\\nCHANNELS_TO_INDEX=\\\\n\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"Path\":\"\\\"d:\\\\\\\\Direct_Link\\\\\\\\.env.example\\\"\"}}]}\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript/00000001.jsonl:{\"step_index\":129,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-01T14:11:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":2891,\"cache_read_tokens\":72800,\"output_tokens\":1181,\"thinking\":\"The deployment guide for Hugging Face Spaces is being created. It details how to deploy using the free tier, beginning with signing up and creating a new Space named 'stream-vault'. The guide specifies the MIT license, Docker SDK, and free hardware configuration. It concludes \n<truncated 30586 of 40472 bytes from the middle of the output>\n\\nAPI_ID=12345678\\nAPI_HASH=your_api_hash_here\\n\\n# Telegram Bot Token (from @BotFather)\\nBOT_TOKEN=1234567890:ABCdefGhIJKlmNoPQRsTUVwxyZ\\n\\n# Private Channel ID for permanent media storage (e.g. -1001234567890)\\nLOG_CHANNEL_ID=-1001234567890\\n\\n# MongoDB Atlas Connection URI\\nMONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\\nDATABASE_NAME=stream_vault\\n\\n# Whitelist Security: Comma-separated list of Telegram User IDs allowed to use the bot\\nALLOWED_USERS=123456789,987654321\\n\\n# Web Server Configuration for Direct Download / Streaming Links (DDL)\\n# For Hugging Face Spaces, PORT is 7860\\nPORT=7860\\nHOST=0.0.0.0\\n# Public base URL used to construct the streaming link in captions\\n# For Hugging Face Spaces: https://<username>-<spacename>.hf.space\\n# For local testing: http://localhost:7860\\nSTREAM_URL=http://localhost:7860\\n\\n# Optional: Comma-separated channel usernames to auto-index on startup\\n# e.g., @public_movie_channel_1, @public_movie_channel_2\\nCHANNELS_TO_INDEX=\\n\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"Path\":\"d:\\\\Direct_Link\\\\.env.example\"}}]}\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl:{\"step_index\":129,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-01T14:11:48Z\",\"input_tokens\":2891,\"cache_read_tokens\":72800,\"output_tokens\":1181,\"thinking\":\"The deployment guide for Hugging Face Spaces is being created. It details how to deploy using the free tier, beginning with signing up and creating a new Space named 'stream-vault'. The guide specifies the MIT license, Docker SDK, and free hardware configuration. It concludes with connecting the Space to a GitHub repository.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"Content\":\"# Deploying StreamVault to Hugging Face Spaces (100% Free)\\n\\nThis guide shows you how to run **stream-vault** 24/7 in the cloud on **Hugging Face Spaces** for free with **zero credit card required**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🎁 What You Get (Free Tier)\\n- **Cost:** \\\\$0.00 / forever\\n- **Credit Card:** Not required\\n- **RAM:** 16 GB\\n- **CPU:** 2 dedicated vCPUs\\n- **Disk:** 50 GB storage buffer\\n- **Public Domain:** Free HTTPS link (`https://<username>-stream-vault.hf.space`) for direct VLC streaming\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3-Minute Deployment Steps\\n\\n### Step 1: Create a Free Hugging Face Account\\n1. Visit [huggingface.co/join](https://huggingface.co/join).\\n2. Sign up using your email or sign in with your GitHub account.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 2: Create a New Docker Space\\n1. Click your profile picture (top right) and select **New Space** (or go to [huggingface.co/new-space](https://huggingface.co/new-space)).\\n2. Fill out the form:\\n   - **Space Name:** `stream-vault`\\n   - **License:** `MIT`\\n   - **Select the Space SDK:** Choose **Docker** -> **Blank**\\n   - **Space Hardware:** Select **Free (2 vCPU · 16 GB RAM)**\\n   - **Visibility:** Public (recommended so the DDL web stream is accessible to VLC/browsers)\\n3. Click **Create Space**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 3: Add Your Secrets (Environment Variables)\\n1. In your newly created Space, navigate to the **Settings** tab.\\n2. Scroll down to **Variables and secrets**.\\n3. Under **Secrets**, click **New secret** for each required key:\\n\\n| Secret Name | Value Example | Description |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `API_ID` | `12345678` | From [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org) |\\n| `API_HASH` | `abcdef123456789...` | From [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org) |\\n| `BOT_TOKEN` | `1234567890:ABCdef...` | From `@BotFather` |\\n| `LOG_CHANNEL_ID` | `-1001234567890` | Your private storage channel ID |\\n| `MONGO_URI` | `mongodb+srv://...` | Free MongoDB Atlas connection string |\\n| `ALLOWED_USERS` | `123456789` | Your personal Telegram User ID |\\n| `STREAM_URL` | `https://<username>-stream-vault.hf.space` | Your Space's public HTTPS URL |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 4: Push Your Code to Hugging Face\\nYou can connect Hugging Face directly to your existing GitHub repo or push with git:\\n\\n```powershell\\n# Add Hugging Face as a git remote (replace <username> with your HF username)\\ngit remote add hf https://huggingface.co/spaces/<your-username>/stream-vault\\n\\n# Push code to build and launch\\ngit push hf main --force\\n```\\n\\nHugging Face will automatically read the `Dockerfile`, install `ffmpeg`, `aria2c`, and launch your bot 24/7!\\n\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"Path\":\"d:\\\\Direct_Link\\\\docs\\\\huggingface-deploy.md\"}}]}\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/credentials-setup-guide.md:MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\ndocs/huggingface-deploy.md:| `MONGO_URI` | `mongodb+srv://...` | Free MongoDB Atlas connection string |\ndocs/setup-guide.md:     mongodb+srv://moviebot:<password>@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\ndocs/setup-guide.md:MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://moviebot:password@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\n"}
