{"step_index":187,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T14:18:08Z","input_tokens":2390,"cache_read_tokens":112322,"output_tokens":718,"content":"Don't worry—**none of your actual private data or real passwords were leaked.** \n\nHere is what that email means and how it was resolved:\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Why GitHub Sent That Email\nGitHub runs automated **Secret Scanning** bots on every repository. When it scanned commit `cc32ac83`, it spotted this **fake example placeholder** inside the setup tutorial at line 91 of `docs/setup-guide.md`:\n\n```text\nMONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://moviebot:password@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/...\n```\n\nBecause that example string strictly matched the pattern of a MongoDB connection string (`username:password@domain`), GitHub’s automated bot flagged it as a potential leaked credential—even though it was only tutorial sample text.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ What Was Fixed\n1. Replaced all sample connection strings across [docs/setup-guide.md](file:///d:/Direct_Link/docs/setup-guide.md), [.env.example](file:///d:/Direct_Link/.env.example), and [credentials-setup-guide.md](file:///d:/Direct_Link/conversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/credentials-setup-guide.md) with safe non-regex placeholders:\n   ```env\n   MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_uri_here\n   ```\n2. Committed and pushed the sanitized files to your repository on `main`.\n\n---\n\n### 📋 How to Close the Alert in GitHub (Takes 10 Seconds)\n1. Click the link in that email: **\"Review secret detected in docs/setup-guide.md#L91\"** (or go to your repo on GitHub → **Security** tab → **Secret scanning alerts**).\n2. Click **Close as...** (top right of the alert).\n3. Select **\"False positive\"** or **\"Used in tests\"**.\n\nThe alert will immediately resolve and turn green.","thinking":"The push triggered a secret scanning alert. Analysis indicates GitHub's automated systems flagged a placeholder database credential pattern within the documentation. The specific pattern identified was a MongoDB connection string containing a username and password. This triggered a security response.\n\n\n"}
