{"step_index":189,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T14:18:59Z","input_tokens":2563,"cache_read_tokens":114187,"output_tokens":1761,"content":"Hugging Face recently updated its policy—**Docker compute Spaces now require a paid PRO plan** (only basic static HTML is free now).\n\nFortunately, you have two **100% free alternatives that do not require any credit card**:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Render.com (Top Free Cloud Pick — 0 Credit Card)\n\n[Render.com](https://render.com) allows you to deploy Docker containers directly from your GitHub repository for free:\n\n* **Cost:** 100% Free (no credit card required on signup).\n* **Setup:**\n  1. Go to [render.com](https://render.com) and click **Sign in with GitHub**.\n  2. Click **New +** (top right) → **Web Service**.\n  3. Select your repository: **`Aswin-2266/stream-vault`**.\n  4. Fill in:\n     - **Name:** `stream-vault`\n     - **Region:** Choose the closest region (e.g., Singapore, Frankfurt, or Oregon)\n     - **Instance Type:** Select **Free**\n  5. Scroll down to **Environment Variables** and add your keys (`API_ID`, `API_HASH`, `BOT_TOKEN`, `LOG_CHANNEL_ID`, `MONGO_URI`, `ALLOWED_USERS`).\n  6. Click **Create Web Service**.\n\nRender will automatically read the `Dockerfile` we already pushed, build it, and give you a free public HTTPS URL (e.g., `https://stream-vault.onrender.com`)!\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Run on Your Local PC + Free Cloudflare Tunnel (Instant)\n\nSince you already have Python on your Windows machine, you can run it right now on your PC:\n* **Zero signups, zero credit cards, zero sleep limits.**\n* You get unlimited disk space and full PC performance.\n* To get a public HTTPS stream link (for playing on your phone or VLC away from home), we can run **Cloudflare Tunnel** (`cloudflared`) with one simple command:\n  ```powershell\n  # Free public HTTPS URL without signup or port forwarding\n  cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:7860\n  ```\n\n---\n\nWhich one would you like to set up: **Render.com (Cloud)** or **Local PC + Cloudflare Tunnel**?","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nHugging Face policy now requires a PRO subscription for Docker and Gradio compute spaces, limiting free options. This change necessitates exploring alternatives that offer free compute without requiring a credit card. Initial research indicates Render and Koyeb as potential candidates, and Render is prioritized because it offers free web services without a credit card requirement.\n\n\nCloudflare Tunnel (`cloudflared`) offers a free HTTPS URL by running the Python script locally, bypassing server limits and signup/credit card requirements. GitHub Codespaces provides free Linux cloud compute with limited core hours. Render's free tier, requiring no credit card, can host a Telegram bot as a web service. Render's free web service has a 15-minute inactivity timeout, which can be mitigated with external ping services.\n\n\n"}
