{"step_index":191,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T14:19:49Z","input_tokens":2942,"cache_read_tokens":115815,"output_tokens":1510,"content":"You are **100% right**. That is a very sharp observation.\n\nRender’s free tier has severe bottlenecks that make it frustrating for movie bots:\n1. **15-Minute Sleep:** When nobody opens the streaming link for 15 minutes, the server shuts down. This breaks Telegram’s connection, so the bot stops responding to messages until someone wakes it up (causing a 50-second delay).\n2. **Tiny 512 MB RAM Limit:** Splitting a 2–4 GB video file with `ffmpeg` or buffering heavy torrent chunks can easily trigger an **Out of Memory (OOM) crash** on Render's free 512 MB container.\n3. **Restricted Ephemeral Disk:** Render does not give you enough free persistent disk space to comfortably download and split 4K or 1080p BluRay releases.\n\n---\n\n### Why Your Local PC is the Best Free Option\n\nRunning the bot directly on your Windows PC solves all of those cloud limitations for **\\$0 and zero credit card**:\n\n| Feature | Render Free Tier | **Your Local PC** |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Storage** | Limited & wiped on restart | **Your entire hard drive** (100 GB – 1 TB+ of free space) |\n| **RAM** | 512 MB (frequent crashes) | **Your full system RAM** (8 GB – 16 GB+) |\n| **Sleep Limits** | Shuts down every 15 minutes | **Zero sleep** — runs as long as your PC is on |\n| **Video Splitting** | Slow / crashes on >2 GB files | **Instant `ffmpeg` stream copying** using your PC CPU |\n| **Credit Card** | No | **No** |\n\n---\n\n### How to Make Your Local PC Behave Like a Cloud Server\n\nTo stream movies on your phone or VLC when you are away from home, you don't even need port forwarding:\n* We run a free tool called **Cloudflare Tunnel** (`cloudflared`).\n* It creates a secure, public HTTPS link (e.g. `https://random-words.trycloudflare.com`) that connects straight to your local bot.\n* You get the benefits of a dedicated cloud server without spending a single dollar or entering a credit card.\n\nShall we set up your `.env` and launch the bot locally right now to test it?","thinking":"The user's observation about Render's storage limitations and auto-